Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: drop OPP vote during PM_SUSPEND_MEM suspend

On OPP-managed Qualcomm PCIe hosts such as SM8550 (where pcie->use_pm_opp
is true and pcie->icc_mem is NULL), qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() previously
gated dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL) behind pm_suspend_target_state !=
PM_SUSPEND_MEM.  During deep sleep (PM_SUSPEND_MEM) with the host still
active (!pcie->pci->suspended), this left the Gen3 x1 OPP active across
suspend, holding a 984,500 kB/s QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS vote on MC0/SH0
(DDR/LLCC) and an rpmhpd_opp_nom corner in SLEEP_SET and preventing
AOSD/CXSD/DDR collapse.

Drop the OPP vote in qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() and restore max OPP in
qcom_pcie_resume_noirq() regardless of PM_SUSPEND_MEM.  On SM8550, the
PCIe OPP table only manages interconnect bandwidth and required-opps (no
clocks or GDSC power-off), and max OPP is restored before
qcom_pcie_icc_opp_update() or any child resume_noirq runs.

---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2206,10 +2206,10 @@
 			if (ret)
 				dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n",
 					ret);
-
-			if (pcie->use_pm_opp)
-				dev_pm_opp_set_opp(pcie->pci->dev, NULL);
 		}
+
+		if (pcie->use_pm_opp)
+			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(pcie->pci->dev, NULL);
 	}
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -2252,15 +2252,15 @@
 		if (ret && ret != -ENODEV && ret != -EIO)
 			goto disable_icc_mem;
 	} else {
+		if (pcie->use_pm_opp) {
+			ret = qcom_pcie_set_max_opp(dev);
+			if (ret) {
+				dev_err(dev, "Failed to set max OPP: %d\n", ret);
+				return ret;
+			}
+		}
+
 		if (pm_suspend_target_state != PM_SUSPEND_MEM) {
-			if (pcie->use_pm_opp) {
-				ret = qcom_pcie_set_max_opp(dev);
-				if (ret) {
-					dev_err(dev, "Failed to set max OPP: %d\n", ret);
-					return ret;
-				}
-			}
-
 			ret = icc_enable(pcie->icc_cpu);
 			if (ret) {
 				dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n",
